    "title": "Pedestrian killed in crash at 4th and West streets in downtown Reno - NewsBreak",
    "text": "A pedestrian died Wednesday, July 9, after being struck by a vehicle in downtown Reno. About 11:20 a.m., Reno police responded to a vehicle vs. pedestrian crash at Fourth and West streets, Reno police said. The pedestrian was transported to a local hospital with life-threatening injuries and later died. The vehicle's driver stayed at the scene and cooperated. Speed and impairment do not appear to be factors, police said. The pedestrian's identity has not been released pending notification of next of kin. Anyone with information is asked to call Reno police at 775-334-2677 or Secret Witness at 775-322-4900, visit secretwitness.com , or text 847411 (TIP) with the keyword “SW.” This article originally appeared on Reno Gazette Journal: Pedestrian killed in crash at 4th and West streets in downtown Reno",
